# Change codes `jfast upgrade --check --json` must report for the project
# scripts/smoke_upgrade.sh generates with the previous release. One per line;
# `#` starts a comment. The set must match exactly: a code missing means a
# detector stopped seeing its case, a code extra means one started seeing a
# case that is not there.
#
# The project: jfast new service shop --with database,auth,tenancy,metrics,rag,queue
# and one module per layout (modular, screaming, hexagonal, layered).
#
# 0.1.0a11 -> 0.1.0a12: nothing. That project has no local storage disk and
# no --unique key over an optional field, the two shapes 0.1.0a12's notes are
# about -- so a code here would be a detector firing on a case that is not
# there. (0.1.0a10 -> 0.1.0a11 expected hexagonal-eager-create-payload.)
